## METHODOLOGICAL INFORMATION\
\
### Data Generation and Simulation\
- Population size: `N = 100,000`  \
- True variance: `1`  \
- Monte Carlo replications: `B = 10,000`  \
- Sample sizes: `n = 2:50`  \
- Sampling: Without replacement from the generated population  \
- Variance estimators:\
  - Divide by `n` (biased estimator)\
  - Divide by `n - 1` (Bessel-corrected, unbiased estimator)\
\
Averages and 5th/95th percentile intervals were computed to compare estimator performance.\
\
### Data Processing\
- Results stored in a data frame\
- Saved as a plot for visualization\
\
### Software Requirements\
- **R (version 4.x or later)**\
- Required packages: none (base R only)\
\
### Quality Assurance\
- `set.seed(123)` used for reproducibility  \
- Large simulation size (10,000 per n) reduces Monte Carlo error\
\
